From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peter Heinrich <heip@zhaw.ch>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 01:00:05 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: add Fullhan FH8626V200 support for an IPC camera board

Board support for a pan/tilt Wi-Fi camera with the Fullhan FH8626V200
SoC (single Cortex-A7), written against Linux 6.18:

- mach-fh8626 machine support and the fullhan/fh8626v200 device tree
  (UART, GIC, timers, pinctrl-single mux, GPIO, I2C0, SPI NOR, USB,
  camera pipeline, actuators)
- clk-fh8626: PMU clock provider with the PLL and gate clocks
- phy-fh8626-usb: USB 2.0 PHY driver for the DWC2 host
  (the SV6355 Wi-Fi module sits on internal USB)
- sc2336: SmartSens SC2336 1080p sensor driver over 2-lane MIPI CSI-2,
  with streaming, exposure and gain controls
- fh8626-camera: V4L2 capture driver for the MIPI/ISP/VPU pipeline,
  with auto exposure, auto white balance, saturation control and
  MJPEG output from the on-chip JPEG encoder; fh8626-isp-bringup
  holds the ISP bring-up helpers
- gpio-stepper: GPIO unipolar stepper motor driver (pan, tilt)
- gpio-ircut: GPIO latching IR-cut filter driver
- fh8626_defconfig

No vendor code or vendor tuning data is used. Register layouts come
from analysis of the hardware and the stock firmware, see the project
documentation.

Signed-off-by: Peter Heinrich <heip@zhaw.ch>
